MyGOFrame local Debian source package
====================================

This packaging targets the Debian release and native architecture used to
build it. The initial binary was validated on Debian sid amd64. FFmpeg ABI
requirements are generated from that system; this is not a Debian stable
binary or an official Debian archive upload.

Run `make deb` from a checkout. tools/build-debian.py copies the source into
an isolated directory, vendors the exact go.mod/go.sum module versions from
the existing Go cache, prepares an orig tarball, and calls dpkg-buildpackage.
The build itself disables network module and Cargo access. Populate the Go
module cache with `go mod download` first if dependencies are not cached.

The pkg.mygoframe.external-toolchains build profile permits an externally
installed Swift 6.3.3 compiler. Debian's `swift` package is OpenStack storage
and is unrelated. Install the official Swift Linux toolchain and set SWIFTC
if it is not on PATH or installed through Swiftly. The toolchain version is
pinned to match the included Swift and ICU runtime notices. The package does not
require the compiler or a Swift installation at runtime. Rust 2024 support
is required; Debian rustc/cargo or an installed rustup toolchain can be used.

To rebuild the prepared source package:

  dpkg-source -x mygoframe_0.1.0-1.dsc
  cd mygoframe-0.1.0
  DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=pkg.mygoframe.external-toolchains dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

The Go executable and Swift facade are built with hardening flags. Swift
standard and Foundation libraries are linked statically into the private
facade. FFmpeg, PipeWire, GTK, and graphics libraries remain system runtime
dependencies. The package includes Swift, Foundation, ICU, Go, and vendored
module license notices under /usr/share/doc/mygoframe/third-party/.

The clean target removes generated files only. It preserves the vendor
snapshot shipped in the orig tarball. No maintainer script changes device
permissions, user groups, or per-user application settings.
